# Getting started

Install Pontia, connect your device to Pontia Cloud, and start using your coding agents from the Remote Dashboard.

<h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>

- Linux with systemd, or macOS 13.5 or later.
- Node.js with npm for the recommended `npx` command. Without Node.js, use the [shell installer](#install-with-the-shell-script).
- At least one coding agent: pi, Codex, Claude Code, or an ACP agent. See [Agent Clients](/docs/agent-clients) for what each one needs.

## Install and initialize Pontia

Run the recommended setup command:

```sh
npx @pontia/cli init
```

This installs Pontia and opens the interactive initializer. If Pontia is already installed, it reuses the installation. You do not need to run `pontia init` again.

The default installation directory is `$HOME/.local/bin`. Add it to your shell `PATH` to run `pontia` commands directly. Set `PONTIA_INSTALL_DIR` to use a different directory.

The npm installation works with npm mirrors and private registries and does not require `curl` or `openssl`. To install without opening the initializer, run `npx @pontia/cli install`.

<h3 id="install-with-the-shell-script">Install with the shell script</h3>

If you prefer to install without Node.js, use the signed release installer. It requires `curl` and `openssl`; see [Linux](/docs/platforms/linux) or [macOS](/docs/platforms/macos) for the full requirements.

```sh
curl -fsSL https://get.pontia.dev/install.sh | sh
"$HOME/.local/bin/pontia" init
```

These commands use the default installation directory. If you set `PONTIA_INSTALL_DIR`, run `pontia init` from that directory instead.

## Complete initialization

The initializer lets you:

1. Select the pi, Codex, and Claude Agent integrations you want.
2. Generate the local dashboard credential.
3. Start the Pontia background service.
4. Sign in to Pontia Cloud and register your device for the Remote Dashboard.

On first initialization, Pontia uses your home directory as the Workspace Browser root. Existing roots are preserved when you run the initializer again.

When prompted to sign in and enable remote access, accept and complete the browser authorization. Select an available edge and confirm your device name. Pontia opens the Remote Dashboard when setup completes.

For an agent or script, follow [Initialization](/docs/initialization) to install Client integrations, start the service, and register remote access with separate commands instead of answering wizard prompts.

## Check the service

```sh
pontia status
```

Use `pontia down` to stop the service and `pontia up` to start it again.

## Update Pontia

Update `pontia` and `pontiad` to the latest signed stable release on Linux or macOS:

```sh
pontia update
```

If the managed service is running, Pontia restarts it and waits for it to become healthy. If replacement or restart fails, Pontia restores the previous binaries and attempts to recover the service.

Open your device's Remote Dashboard and follow the [Dashboard guide](/docs/dashboard) to activate a Workspace and start your first Session. If device registration is not yet complete, finish the [remote access setup](/docs/remote-access) first.
